# SHACL shapes for provenance-based work-item co-occurrence (quipu#37).
#
# The substrate for auditable, DETERMINISTIC work-item co-occurrence — "what work
# touched this entity, and what else did that work touch" — as a graph query over
# typed provenance edges, NOT a statistical mine (that stays in Bobbin). Hank
# promotes the raw provenance at commit time (hank #18 / FR-19); Quipu aggregates.
#
# The provenance chain (predicates already in aegis-ontology.shapes.ttl):
#
#     Bead  <--aegis:implements--  GitCommit  --aegis:modifies-->  CodeModule|CodeSymbol
#            (commit implements bead)         (commit touched entity, = #18's edge)
#
# Two work-items CO-OCCUR iff they share a touched entity:
#
#     ?cA aegis:implements ?beadA ; aegis:modifies ?e .
#     ?cB aegis:modifies ?e ; aegis:implements ?beadB .   ->  beadA co-occurs with beadB
#
# Run it via the /cooccurrence endpoint (quipu::tool_cooccurrence), or directly in
# SPARQL. Bitemporal by construction: a valid_at scopes it to "as of <date>".
#
# This file adds only the ONE edge the chain was missing — epic membership — so
# an epic touches the union of its beads' entities. `aegis:modifies` and
# `aegis:implements` are confirmed (not redefined) here; their PropertyShapes live
# in aegis-ontology.shapes.ttl and stay permissive per hank-spec §9.2
# ("start permissive, tighten deliberately").
#
# Load via POST /shapes:
#   curl -s localhost:3030/shapes -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#     -d '{"action":"load","name":"provenance","turtle":"<contents>"}'

@prefix sh:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix aegis:  <http://aegis.gastown.local/ontology/> .

# ── contains: Epic/Bead → Bead ─────────────────────────────────────
# Work-item hierarchy: an epic (or parent bead) contains child beads, so it
# touches the union of their entities. Range is a Bead; domain (epic vs bead) is
# left open — an epic is just a Bead with children in the aegis model.

# TARGETED so the shape can actually fire: without a target an
# unreferenced PropertyShape validates nothing — this file's only shape was
# "valid" by construction, vacuously, from the day it loaded. targetSubjectsOf
# binds every node that ASSERTS a contains edge, and nothing else: measured 0
# such subjects live on 2026-07-23, so this arms the rule without adding a
# single violation. The first contains edge with a non-Bead object now fails
# instead of passing silently.
aegis:ContainsShape a sh:PropertyShape ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf aegis:contains ;
    sh:path aegis:contains ;
    sh:class aegis:Bead .
